{"chunk_id":"R1-2301126-001","collection":"ran1_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Ericsson"],"tdocNumber":"R1-2301126","title":"[Draft] Reply LS on default CBR configuration"},"point_id":"4966122685183360048"}
119bis [Proposal 18] Changes related to default CBR parameters are postponed to next meeting. (6/10) [Session chair]: Check companies’ understanding (assuming R17 default CBR is configured) Case 1: partial sensing, R17 normal pool, R17 default CBR – partial Case 2a: random selection, R17 normal pool, R17 default CBR – random Case 2b: random selection, R16/17 exceptional pool, R16 default CBR Case 3: full sensing, R16/17 normal pool, R16 default CBR or invalid case? Case 1, 2a, 2b are confirmed. Case 3 will be revisited next meeting. RAN2 further discussed Case-3 above at RAN2#120 yet failed to reach consensus on whether or not it is valid. Therefore, RAN2 kindly requests RAN1 to provide answer to Q1 below. Reply to Q1: From RAN1 perspective, in general when the UE is performing full sensing and the full sensing results are available it is reasonable to expect that it has already CBR measurements. However, since CBR and the full sensing operation are two independent mechanisms and UE capabilities as indicated in TS38.822 it might be possible that CBR measurements under full sensing are not available, and the UE has to rely on a default CBR value. 2. Actions: RAN1 kindly requests RAN2 to take the above information into consideration for their future work. 3. Dates of Next RAN WG1 Meetings: TSG RAN WG1 Meeting #112-bis-e 17 April– 26 April 2023 Online TSG RAN WG1 Meeting #113 22 May– 26 May 2023 Incheon, South Korea

